IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-solvency`

-- Tests for sg-solvency.l4 (s 7A). Expected values are worked out by hand from the subsection named beside each assertion.

§ `Fixtures`

-- Columns of `Solvency statement`, in DECLARE order: the proposal; its date; by the directors; opinion (a); opinion (b)(i) winding up
-- within 12 months; opinion (b)(ii) debts as they fall due; opinion (c) now; opinion (c) after the proposal; winding up intended;
-- number of directors; number who signed; accompanied by the auditor's report.
`the date of the statement` MEANS Date 1 6 2026

`a complete statement, no winding up intended, all three directors signed` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a complete statement where winding up is intended` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement for financial assistance, otherwise complete` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a giving of financial assistance under section 76(9A) or (9B)`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 2, 2, FALSE
`a statement for a reduction of share capital, otherwise complete` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a reduction of share capital under section 78B or 78C`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 1, 1, FALSE
`a complete statement for some other proposal` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `some other proposal`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement not made by the directors` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement without opinion (a)` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement with the wrong opinion (b): winding up intended, but only the going-concern opinion` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement with the wrong opinion (b): no winding up intended, but only the winding-up opinion` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement without opinion (c) as at its date` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a statement without opinion (c) after the proposal` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, 3, 3, FALSE
`a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with the auditor's report` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 2, TRUE
`a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with no auditor's report` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 2, FALSE
`a complete statement signed by all three directors, with the auditor's report too` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 3, TRUE
`a complete statement signed by nobody, with no auditor's report` MEANS
    `Solvency statement` OF `a redemption of preference shares out of capital under section 70`, `the date of the statement`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 3, 0, FALSE

§ `Section 7A(1): the content`

#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a complete statement, no winding up intended, all three directors signed` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a complete statement where winding up is intended` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement for financial assistance, otherwise complete` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement for a reduction of share capital, otherwise complete` EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Each missing element is a "no": the definition says "means".
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement not made by the directors` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement without opinion (a)` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement with the wrong opinion (b): winding up intended, but only the going-concern opinion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement with the wrong opinion (b): no winding up intended, but only the winding-up opinion` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement without opinion (c) as at its date` EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a statement without opinion (c) after the proposal` EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered: the definition is "in relation to" the three proposals only.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement has the content the section requires` `a complete statement for some other proposal` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1)(b) the statement gives the opinion that the intention calls for` `a complete statement where winding up is intended` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1)(b) the statement gives the opinion that the intention calls for` `a statement with the wrong opinion (b): winding up intended, but only the going-concern opinion` EQUALS FALSE

§ `Section 7A(2): the form`

-- (a) a company exempt from audit: every director must sign; the auditor's report does not help.
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement, no winding up intended, all three directors signed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with the auditor's report` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with no auditor's report` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (b) a company not exempt: every director signs, or the auditor's report accompanies it.
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement, no winding up intended, all three directors signed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with the auditor's report` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with no auditor's report` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by all three directors, with the auditor's report too` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by nobody, with no auditor's report` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(2) the statement is in the form the subsection requires` `a complete statement signed by nobody, with no auditor's report` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE

§ `Section 7A(1) as a whole: content and form`

#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a complete statement, no winding up intended, all three directors signed` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a complete statement, no winding up intended, all three directors signed` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Complete content, wrong form: for the exempt company, two of three signatures is not enough; for the audited company the report cures it.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with the auditor's report` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a complete statement signed by two of three directors, with the auditor's report` FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Right form, wrong content.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a statement without opinion (a)` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a statement not made by the directors` TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not covered.
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a complete statement for some other proposal` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(1) the statement is a solvency statement` `a complete statement for some other proposal` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Sections 7A(3), (4), (5): forming the opinion`

#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the directors have formed the opinion as the subsection requires` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(3) the directors have formed the opinion as the subsection requires` FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(a): both limbs.
#ASSERT `s 7A(4)(a) the directors have had regard to what the paragraph requires` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4)(a) the directors have had regard to what the paragraph requires` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4)(a) the directors have had regard to what the paragraph requires` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4)(a) the directors have had regard to what the paragraph requires` FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- (4)(b): a grant limited by its own words; outside the limit is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 7A(4)(b) the directors may rely on the valuation or estimate` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(4)(b) the directors may rely on the valuation or estimate` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5): the two matters named; any other is not covered.
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the directors may take the matter into account in valuing a contingent liability` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the directors may take the matter into account in valuing a contingent liability` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `s 7A(5) the directors may take the matter into account in valuing a contingent liability` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 7A(6): the offence`

-- All three elements: a director, made the statement, had no reasonable grounds.
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- Reasonable grounds: this subsection makes the director guilty of nothing. (Whether the company later failed is not an element.)
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Not a director, or did not make the statement.
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the director is guilty of the offence this subsection creates` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The penalty: a fine not exceeding $100,000 or imprisonment not exceeding 3 years or both.
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (`s 7A(6) penalty` OF 100000, 3, TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 7A(6) the most the director may be sentenced to on conviction` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Regulative rules: traces`

-- s 7A(3): a duty with no time limit and no stated consequence (NOTES.md: Rules with no breach path).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 7A(3) a director must take into account all liabilities` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 7A(3) take into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)` AT 3
-- Even a very late act reads FULFILLED: no deadline exists to miss.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 7A(3) a director must take into account all liabilities` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 7A(3) take into account all liabilities of the company (including contingent liabilities)` AT 4000
-- Nothing done: the duty still stands.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 7A(3) a director must take into account all liabilities` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    -- no events

-- s 7A(4)(a): both acts, in order.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 7A(4)(a) a director must have regard to the financial statements` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 7A(4)(a)(i) have regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5)` AT 1
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 7A(4)(a)(ii) have regard to all other circumstances that the directors know or ought to know affect the value of the company's assets and liabilities` AT 2
-- Only the first: the second duty is outstanding.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 7A(4)(a) a director must have regard to the financial statements` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 7A(4)(a)(i) have regard to the most recent financial statements of the company that comply with section 201(2) and (5)` AT 1

-- s 7A(6): the prohibition. The forbidden act reaches BREACH.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 7A(6) a director must not make a solvency statement without reasonable grounds` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Director "Dee" DOES `s 7A(6) make a solvency statement without having reasonable grounds for the opinions expressed in it` AT 5
-- No act: nothing has been breached; the prohibition stands.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 7A(6) a director must not make a solvency statement without reasonable grounds` "Dee" AT 0 WITH
    -- no events
